{"path":"cargo/reference/registry-authentication.html","title":"Registry Authentication","description":"Cargo authenticates to registries with credential providers. These credential providers are external executables or built-in providers that Cargo uses to store and retrieve credentials.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"registry-authentication","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registry Authentication"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo authenticates to registries with credential providers. These credential providers are external executables or built-in providers that Cargo uses to store and retrieve credentials."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Using alternative registries with authentication "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"requires"}]},{"type":"text","value":" a credential provider to be configured to avoid unknowingly storing unencrypted credentials on disk. For historical reasons, public (non-authenticated) registries do not require credential provider configuration, and the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:token"},{"type":"text","value":" provider is used if no providers are configured."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo also includes platform-specific providers that use the operating system to securely store tokens. The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:token"},{"type":"text","value":" provider is also included which stores credentials in unencrypted plain text in the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/config.html#credentials","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"credentials"}]},{"type":"text","value":" file."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"recommended-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recommended configuration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It’s recommended to configure a global credential provider list in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"$CARGO_HOME/config.toml"},{"type":"text","value":" which defaults to:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Windows: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"%USERPROFILE%\\.cargo\\config.toml"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unix: "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"~/.cargo/config.toml"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This recommended configuration uses the operating system provider, with a fallback to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:token"},{"type":"text","value":" to look in Cargo’s "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/config.html#credentials","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"credentials"}]},{"type":"text","value":" file or environment variables:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"# ~/.cargo/config.toml\n[registry]\nglobal-credential-providers = [\"cargo:token\", \"cargo:libsecret\", \"cargo:macos-keychain\", \"cargo:wincred\"]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that later entries have higher precedence. See "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/config.html#registryglobal-credential-providers","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"registry.global-credential-providers"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for more details."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some private registries may also recommend a registry-specific credential-provider. Check your registry’s documentation to see if this is the case."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"built-in-providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Built-in providers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cargo includes several built-in credential providers. The available built-in providers may change in future Cargo releases (though there are currently no plans to do so)."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"cargotoken","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:token"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses Cargo’s "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/config.html#credentials","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"credentials"}]},{"type":"text","value":" file to store tokens unencrypted in plain text. When retrieving tokens, checks the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"CARGO_REGISTRIES_<NAME>_TOKEN"},{"type":"text","value":" environment variable. If this credential provider is not listed, then the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"*_TOKEN"},{"type":"text","value":" environment variables will not work."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"cargowincred","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:wincred"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the Windows Credential Manager to store tokens."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The credentials are stored as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo-registry:<index-url>"},{"type":"text","value":" in the Credential Manager under “Windows Credentials”."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"cargomacos-keychain","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:macos-keychain"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses the macOS Keychain to store tokens."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Keychain Access app can be used to view stored tokens."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"cargolibsecret","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:libsecret"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses "},{"type":"link","href":"https://wiki.gnome.org/Projects/Libsecret","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"libsecret"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to store tokens."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Any password manager with libsecret support can be used to view stored tokens. The following are a few examples (non-exhaustive):"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://wiki.gnome.org/Projects/GnomeKeyring","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"GNOME Keyring"}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://apps.kde.org/kwalletmanager5/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"KDE Wallet Manager"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (since KDE Frameworks 5.97.0)"}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://keepassxc.org/","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"KeePassXC"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (since 2.5.0)"}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"cargotoken-from-stdout-command-args","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo:token-from-stdout <command> <args>"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Launch a subprocess that returns a token on stdout. Newlines will be trimmed."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The process inherits the user’s stdin and stderr."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"It should exit 0 on success, and nonzero on error."}]},{"children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-login.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo login"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-logout.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo logout"}]},{"type":"text","value":" are not supported and return an error if used."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following environment variables will be provided to the executed command:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"CARGO"},{"type":"text","value":" — Path to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo"},{"type":"text","value":" binary executing the command."}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"CARGO_REGISTRY_INDEX_URL"},{"type":"text","value":" — The URL of the registry index."}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"CARGO_REGISTRY_NAME_OPT"},{"type":"text","value":" — Optional name of the registry. Should not be used as a lookup key."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Arguments will be passed on to the subcommand."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"credential-plugins","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Credential plugins"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For credential provider plugins that follow Cargo’s "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/credential-provider-protocol.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"credential provider protocol"}]},{"type":"text","value":", the configuration value should be a string with the path to the executable (or the executable name if on the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PATH"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, to install "},{"type":"link","href":"https://crates.io/crates/cargo-credential-1password","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"cargo-credential-1password"}]},{"type":"text","value":" from crates.io do the following:"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install the provider with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo install cargo-credential-1password"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the config, add to (or create) "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"registry.global-credential-providers"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"toml","code":"[registry]\nglobal-credential-providers = [\"cargo:token\", \"cargo-credential-1password --account my.1password.com\"]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The values in "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"global-credential-providers"},{"type":"text","value":" are split on spaces into path and command-line arguments. To define a global credential provider where the path or arguments contain spaces, use the "},{"type":"link","href":"cargo/reference/config.html#credential-alias","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"[credential-alias]"},{"type":"text","value":" table"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}}
